{"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ReactorRouter\/init()"],"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ReactorRouter\/boundEvents"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ReactorRouter\/fallback(_:)","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ReactorRouter\/handler()","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ReactorRouter\/on(_:_:)","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ReactorRouter\/on(eventNamed:_:)"],"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ReactorRouter","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"§22.10’s handler is ONE function from an event to one answer, which is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"right shape for the wire and the wrong shape for the code. A reactor"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"registered for three events opens with a "},{"code":"switch","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"code":"event.event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"switch is where two defects live. The first is cheap: a misspelled event name"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"binds nothing and is discovered as an event that never fires. The second is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not — it is the "},{"code":"default:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" arm that returns "},{"code":".allow","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on behalf of code that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"never ran, which is §22.10 rule 2’s defect relocated into user code where the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rule does not reach it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A BUILDER RATHER THAN AN ATTRIBUTE"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":", and §22.14 records why: a Swift","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reactor handler is an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"async"},{"text":" closure, and collecting ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"async"},{"text":" members by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reflection costs a runtime dependency an SDK should not add to hand out an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attribute. A builder type-checks the closure against","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"(ReactorEvent) async throws -> ReactorAnswer"},{"text":" at compile time, which is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stricter than what the reflection would have bought. Kotlin made the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"trade for the same reason.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"PURE SUGAR."}]},{"type":"text","text":" It opens no connection, consumes no queue, verifies no event,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"signs no reply and interprets no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timeout_ms"},{"type":"text","text":"; its output is exactly the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"handler the runtime accepts (rule 1)."}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Bind one handler per event and let the SDK compose them into the single"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"handler "},{"isAct